# Livewire Performance
- `render()` runs on every interaction: audit every re-render path for N+1 — eager load in `render()` or computed properties, never rely on a one-time load in `mount()` for query-backed data.
- Use `#[Computed]` for derived data — cached per request, not serialized into the payload; add `persist: true` only for genuinely expensive cross-request values.
- Mark heavy components `#[Lazy]` with a meaningful `placeholder()` so initial page load skips their queries.
- Budget polling: `wire:poll` cost = requests × interval × concurrent users. Use the longest viable interval, `wire:poll.visible`, and prefer events/broadcasting over polling for rare changes.
- Keep public property payloads minimal — they serialize into every request/response round-trip. Store ids and scalars, not full models/collections; rehydrate via computed properties.
- Never bind `.live` to inputs that trigger queries without debounce/throttle.
- Paginate lists with `WithPagination`; never hold an unbounded collection in component state.
- Prefer `wire:navigate` and skip re-rendering static subtrees with `wire:ignore` where safe.
